student_answer:
1. Match: The inference engine examines all the rules in the database to see which ones match the current facts introduced by the user or already existing in the system; 
2. Conflict Resolution: When multiple rules match simultaneously, the system must decide which one to apply first. This stage is crucial for avoiding infinite loops or contradictory conclusions;
3. Execution: After choosing the optimal rule, the system "fires" it (i.e., executes). This means that the THEN part of the rule becomes a new fact in working memory.
